    "Department for Work and Pensions systems remain offline following a cyber incident.",
    "A former UK chief technology officer suspects the outage was caused by a cyber attack, though this is unconfirmed.",
    "The government reports that pension and benefit payments are continuing despite the platform downtime."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The United Kingdom's Department for Work and Pensions (DWP) has taken several digital systems offline following a reported cyber incident. The disruption has impacted access to portals for services including Universal Credit and Personal Independence Payment (PIP). While government officials have stated there is currently no evidence that personal data has been compromised, the outage has persisted for multiple days. A former UK chief technology officer has publicly expressed strong suspicions that the disruption is the result of a cyber attack, though the government has not officially confirmed the nature or source of the incident. Despite the widespread loss of portal access, authorities have maintained that payments to beneficiaries will continue to be processed. The incident has drawn significant attention due to the scale of the service impact on millions of people who rely on DWP support.",
